# Audit — copy to docs/AUDIT.md and customize for your project.

When you ask for **an audit**, that means **everything** — one pass, closed scope. Report **only Fix and Improve**.

Pair with **`docs/AUDIT.config.json`** (from `AUDIT.config.json.template`).

**Reference:** `pack/templates/docs/AUDIT.app.reference.md` and `pack/audit/behavior-fixture/docs/AUDIT.md`.

## Coverage contract

- No partial audits, Phase A/B, or "extend coverage later"
- **One audit, three steps** — never `-SkipTests` for step 1
- Domain map gaps → **Fix** (auto-detected by `run_audit_core.ps1`)
- Audit file drift → **Fix** (auto-detected by `sync-audit-system.ps1 -VerifyOnly`)

## How to run

```bat
run_audit.cmd
scripts\verify_semantic_audit.cmd
scripts\finalize_audit.cmd
```

| Step | Command | Who |
|------|---------|-----|
| 1 — Machine | `run_audit.cmd` | Tooling (full tests) |
| 2 — Semantic | Edit `docs/.audit_semantic_report.json` + `verify_semantic_audit.cmd` | Auditor |
| 3 — Finalize | `scripts\finalize_audit.cmd` | Tooling (no retest when manifest proof valid) |

Re-run **full `run_audit.cmd`** only if git HEAD or source tree changed since step 1 (no-git repos use a tree fingerprint — re-run step 1 when source changed).

## Report format

**Fix** and **Improve** only. If none: **Nothing found.**

## After an audit

Fix items, then re-run step 1 if tests need refreshing; otherwise update semantic report and **`finalize_audit.cmd`**.

## Checklist sections

Every section here must be reviewed in `docs/.audit_semantic_report.json` before an audit can pass — that is the point of the list. Add, rename, or split sections (letters A–N) as the project grows; sections D–K are the code domains referenced by the domain map below. Deleting a section removes it from the gate, so delete only what genuinely does not apply.

### A. Test harness
- `run_tests.bat` passes and covers every test file in `tests/`
- Audit engine self-test passes on this machine

### B. Scope / inventory
- `docs/.audit_inventory.json` counts acknowledged in the semantic report
- No production module missing from the domain map below
- **Folder glossary** present and matching the tree - a reader can tell build output from build input, from runtime user data, from release archive
- No **in-repo duplicate** of a released copy when policy says the archive lives outside the repo
- No script **recreates** a path this checklist forbids - if it does, the script or this checklist is wrong
- Ephemeral dirs (`build`, `dist`) noted as **expected after a build**, not silently deleted and forgotten

### C. Documentation
- `README.md` describes what the project does and how to run it
- `AGENTS.md` and `docs/AUDIT.md` match how the project actually works

### D. Core modules
- Entry module and its helpers behave as documented
- No dead or duplicated logic left behind by recent changes

### K. Security / data handling
- No secrets, tokens, or credentials in tracked files
- No unsafe deserialization (`yaml.load` without `SafeLoader`, `pickle.loads`)

### L. Agent wiring
- `AGENTS.md` points agents at `run_audit.cmd` and `run_tests.bat`
- Audit artifacts (`docs/.audit_*`) are gitignored
- Audit files match the pack: `scripts\sync_audit_system.cmd` reports no drift

